/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  pump10_supercritical_outlet
  ===========================

  What it shows: a pump whose DISCHARGE PRESSURE lies above the fluid's
  critical pressure.  Water on IF97 is pumped from 1 bar, 298.15 K to
  300 bar (critical pressure 220.64 bar), eta = 0.65.

  Above p_c there is no saturation line, so the pump does not ask for
  T_sat(P_out) (IF97 region 4 refuses it above 22.064 MPa); the outlet is
  single-phase compressed liquid and the liquid-branch ceiling check is
  skipped.  Before the fix this case stopped with "IF97 region 4: Tsat(p)
  called at p = 30 MPa", a refusal of a perfectly good state.

  Hand check: w_real = v dP / eta with v ~ 1.8e-5 m3/mol, dP = 2.99e7 Pa
  gives ~ 830 J/mol; the part stored as pressure is v(1 - alpha T) dP, the
  rest heats the liquid by about 4-5 K (T_out ~ 302.7 K, external review:
  302.723 K).  The run's energy balance closes: W_shaft = F (h_out - h_in).
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/// stream state lives on disk in 0/ (per-stream files); flowsheetDict is TOPOLOGY only

units
(
    {
        name        pump10;
        type        pump;
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( out );

        operation
        {
            P_out     300.0 bar;         // above the critical pressure (220.64 bar)
            eta       0.65;              // pump efficiency
        }
    }
);
